/// The doubling `P = 2P` of a point on P-384 in Jacobian coordinates, for `a = -3` (dbl-2001-b, with `Z' = 2YZ`). Coordinates are numbers of 6 64-bit words (`48` bytes), little-endian, in Montgomery's form modulo P-384's prime `p`, and a point is three at consecutive offsets of `ws`: `P` at bytes 736 to 879, `Q` at bytes 1024 to 1167. The function reads `p` at byte 64. The function's own working space is bytes 880 to 1023, 1168 to 1455 and 4048 to 4095 of `ws`; every other byte of `ws` but the result's keeps its value.
///
/// Contract: `doubleContract`, `addCachedContract`, `addAffineContract` or `projAddAffineContract` of `VG.Spec.Weierstrass.PointOps.Curve`. Constant time: only the pointer may affect timing.
///
/// The function keeps `rbp` and `r12`–`r15` in `xmm0`–`xmm4` (`movq`) while it runs, and runs the code `vg_ecdsa_p384_verify_adx` inlined before it called it: the sum into `D` (bytes 880 to 1023), with the temporaries `t0`–`t5` (bytes 1168 to 1455), copied back to `P`, its field operations those of P-384's verification on six 64-bit words modulo `p` read at byte 64, multiplied with BMI2's `mulx` and ADX's `adcx` and `adox` (two carry chains at once) and reduced by six rounds of `u p` for `u = t₀ (2³² + 1) mod 2⁶⁴`, the products' temporary area bytes 4048 to 4095.
///
/// Doubling dbl-2001-b for `a = -3` with `Z' = 2YZ` as a product: eight products, no branch.
///
